  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-05-01T04:36:48.726Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With the ability to enable \"Synchronize Position\" on a UdonBehaviour, we now lack the ability to move this object without lerping it.\nThe current way it's working is that if we move a object over a greater distance (changing the transform position), it will be instant for the owner of the object but any remote client will see the object \"float\" towards the targeted transform.\nWith that I request a way to move synced objects with or without lerp enabled.\n---\nYes this can be done by not using Udon Sync Position, but by syncing the position and rotation using Sync on variables and updating it on the behaviour itself.\nHaving a native way to \"teleport\" a object is much better and much more reliable, even better on the overall performance.",
